  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">New Task Order Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this task order is to avoid Ant deficiency Act violations by having a reserve of money available for USDA to charge staff time and other MCC-related expenses that accrue in the time before a specific task order is signed to allocate funding for that purpose. In general, USDA staff charge time to this account while working on task order development for MCC. This includes budget drafting, editing and disseminating a scope of work, and meeting with MCC staff as appropriate. This task order also covers USDA time spent on more general MCC program tasks that relate to the whole interagency agreement rather than to any specific task order.</narrative>
  </description>
